@startuml write_boundary
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' write_boundary — v29.0 Slice 1: proposal → validation → confirmation →
' effect, with no model anywhere. The debug panel plays the model; Slice 2
' swaps the proposer and changes NOTHING to the right of it.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The write boundary (v29.0) — nothing left of the tap can touch data

rectangle "PROPOSER\n(Slice 1: the debug injector.\nSlice 2: the intake model.\nEither way: outside the boundary)" as proposer
rectangle "verbs::Proposal\nclosed verb set, per-role\n(Intake → SetTaskDetails;\nNudge/CheckIn → nothing)" as proposal
rectangle "HandleMap (per turn)\n[T1] → id, invented\nhandles die to \"\"" as handles
rectangle "validate()\nrole ∧ handle ∧ open target\n∧ additive ∧ sane —\nreason in owner's words" as validate
rectangle "ProposalCard\nApply / Discard\nsummary from FIELDS,\nnever proposer prose" as card
rectangle "data.json copied aside\n(.pre-apply — §B's\ncheap insurance)" as aside
rectangle "apply()\nRE-validates at the tap,\nthen EXISTING doors only:\nsetTaskSize, setTaskDueDate" as apply
rectangle "AppData\n(86+ domain tests\nalready guard the doors)" as appdata
rectangle "Transcript receipt\n\"✓ Applied: …\" (localOnly —\nnever sent to any model)" as receipt

proposer --> proposal : composes
proposal --> validate
handles --> validate : resolves T1
validate --> card : verdict rendered\n(born-broken → dead Apply)
card --> aside : the owner's tap
aside --> apply
apply --> appdata : doors, not\nnew capability
apply --> receipt : on ok

note bottom of card
  The amber moment: everything left of this
  box is words. Discard → settle, nothing
  happens, nothing is recorded.
end note

note bottom of apply
  The stale-card rule: the world may change
  while the card waits (owner fills the field
  by hand) — the tap re-validates and refuses
  politely rather than overwrite.
end note

@enduml
